  "result": "The gate returned **OK** on the second of six runs: all 7 witnesses pass and 9 names are used. The rule needs no other rule.\n\n**What the rule says**\n- **Who:** ego must be a vehicle under `DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle`.\n- **When it applies:** ego is on a roadway of a highway that has a median or divider on it.\n- **Exceptions:** it does not apply while ego is inside a median opening (a crossover) or inside an intersection on that highway.\n- **The duty:** every median or divider on that highway must be on ego's left, meaning a positive lateral offset from ego. That puts ego on the right-hand roadway.\n\n**Gate runs**\n1. **VACUOUS:** I had also written the exceptions into the duty. They changed no witness there, because the \"when it applies\" part already excludes those moments. I removed them from the duty. They now appear only in \"when it applies\", which matches the node's wording (\"not judged at an observation…\").\n2. **OK.**\n\n**Choices I made where the node left room**\n- **Exceptions not repeated in the duty.** One limit follows: if ego were on two divided highways at once and only one had an exception, the duty would still check the excepted one. None of the witnesses builds that case.\n- **\"Driven upon\" means on a roadway.** The d2 note also mentions being on the median, but I followed the node's own \"when it applies\" statement, which requires a roadway. Driving inside the dividing section is d5, which belongs to a different node.\n- **No narrowings declared.**\n\n**Witnesses**\n- The five the node planned (forbid, permit, idle, blind, branch_1) are built as described.\n- I added **branch_2** (not applicable): ego on the wrong roadway but inside an intersection on the highway. This tests the intersection exception.\n- I added **branch_3** (violated): the same scene as branch_1 but with no opening in the median. This tests the opening condition.\n\n`task_result.md` is in the working directory.",
